{
  peppy_schema: "contract/v1",
  manifest: {
    name: "simulation_clock",
    tag: "v1",
    description: [
      "The clock of a simulation and the hold on it: what simulated time it is now, whether the simulation is paused, and a step of a paused simulation by a chosen duration.",
      "`now` is on the same clock as the stamps of the simulation's messages, so a caller compares a stamp with it and knows how old the stamp is.",
      "While paused, simulated time stands still: the engine steps no physics, publishes no clock tick and none of the streams of its state, and keeps answering every service and every scene command, so a world can be arranged with nothing moving. A step advances the simulation by a duration, rounded up to whole physics steps, at the engine's normal pace, and leaves it paused. A robot that runs on wall time cannot move while the simulation is paused: its limbs go silent, and a move in flight fails. Resume before a robot moves.",
      "Before the clock has a time, get_clock and set_paused give an error reply with `precondition_failed`.",
    ],
  },
  interfaces: {
    services: [
      {
        name: "get_clock",
        description: "Give the simulated time now and whether the simulation is paused.",
        response_message_format: {
          now: { $type: "time", $description: "The simulated time now, on the clock the simulation's messages are stamped with." },
          paused: "bool",
        },
      },
      {
        name: "set_paused",
        description: "Pause the simulation, or resume it. Setting the state it is already in gives the response and changes nothing.",
        request_message_format: {
          paused: "bool",
        },
        response_message_format: {
          now: { $type: "time", $description: "The simulated time now." },
          paused: { $type: "bool", $description: "The state after the call." },
        },
      },
    ],
    actions: [
      {
        name: "step",
        description: "Advance a paused simulation by duration_s of simulated time, at the engine's normal pace, and leaves it paused. The goal completes when the last physics step of the duration has run. A step waits for the step before it to end. The step is refused with `precondition_failed` while the simulation runs. A resume, or a build of simulation_world, that comes before the last physics step of the duration has run ends the step cancelled, with a reason that names it. A cancelled step gives the reason of the cancel and its result. The action gives no feedback. The result gives the simulated time when the goal ended.",
        goal_service: {
          request_message_format: {
            duration_s: { $type: "f64", $description: "How far to advance (s), rounded up to whole physics steps. A duration that is not finite, not above 0, or above 30 is refused with `rejected`." },
          },
        },
        result_service: {
          response_message_format: {
            now: { $type: "time", $description: "The simulated time when the goal ended." },
          },
        },
      },
    ],
  },
}
